<section class="bs-hero"><div class="bs-w bs-hero-g"><div class="bs-hero-t"><p class="bs-sig">made for one</p><h1>The art of the <em>bespoke</em> suit</h1><p class="bs-lead">A calm, independent guide to tailoring: what bespoke really means, how a suit is cut and fitted by hand, and how to choose the right cloth and size before you ever visit a tailor.</p>
<div class="bs-hero-a"><a class="bs-btn" href="#size">Find your jacket size</a><a class="bs-lnk" href="how-a-bespoke-suit-is-made-guide.html">See how it&rsquo;s made</a></div><dl class="bs-stats"><div><dt>Measurements</dt><dd><span data-count="30">0</span>+</dd></div><div><dt>Fittings</dt><dd><span data-count="3">0</span></dd></div><div><dt>Hours of handwork</dt><dd><span data-count="60">0</span>+</dd></div></dl></div>
<div class="bs-hero-v"><figure class="bs-arch"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1769107263443-ef16af85070a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=680&q=75" alt="a man in a pinstripe suit holding a jacket indoors" width="520" height="680" fetchpriority="high"></figure><div class="bs-draft"><svg viewBox="0 0 300 360" class="bs-jk" aria-hidden="true"><path class="ch" d="M150 30L108 40L60 62L40 150L32 320L120 336L150 300L180 336L268 320L260 150L240 62L192 40z"/><path class="ch ch2" d="M108 40L150 150L192 40M150 150L150 300M120 110L150 150L180 110"/><path class="ch ch3" d="M70 210h40M190 210h40M76 120h28"/><g class="bt"><circle cx="150" cy="200" r="5"/><circle cx="150" cy="240" r="5"/></g><g class="mk"><path d="M20 60v260"/><path d="M14 60h12M14 320h12"/><text x="8" y="196" transform="rotate(-90 8 196)">LENGTH</text></g></svg><p>Chalk draft &middot; No. 0427</p></div><span class="bs-swatch" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></div></section>

<section class="bs-s bs-an"><div class="bs-w bs-an-g"><div class="bs-an-v"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794344811358-200d8f2e9d00?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=560&q=75" alt="a close up of a red blazer pocket flap and its stitching" width="560" height="560" loading="lazy"></figure><button type="button" class="bs-pin" style="left:36%;top:24%" data-k="0" aria-label="Lapel"><span>1</span></button><button type="button" class="bs-pin" style="left:70%;top:10%" data-k="1" aria-label="Shoulder"><span>2</span></button><button type="button" class="bs-pin" style="left:18%;top:56%" data-k="2" aria-label="Buttonholes"><span>3</span></button><button type="button" class="bs-pin" style="left:74%;top:60%" data-k="3" aria-label="Pockets"><span>4</span></button></div><div><p class="bs-ey">Anatomy of a jacket</p><h2 class="rv">Four details that give it away</h2><p class="bs-p">Tap a number to read about each detail. On a well-made jacket these are cut and finished by hand.</p><ol class="bs-an-l" id="an-l"><li data-k="0" class="on"><b>Lapel</b><p>Notch, peak or shawl. Cut and rolled by hand, it should lie flat without pressing.</p></li><li data-k="1"><b>Shoulder</b><p>Natural, roped or structured. The single hardest part to alter later.</p></li><li data-k="2"><b>Buttonholes</b><p>Hand-sewn with silk twist; working cuff buttons are a hallmark of the craft.</p></li><li data-k="3"><b>Pockets</b><p>Flap, jetted or patch. Each choice changes how formal the jacket reads.</p></li></ol></div></div></section>

<section class="bs-s bs-sz" id="size"><div class="bs-w"><div class="bs-sh"><p class="bs-ey">Tool one</p><h2 class="rv">Jacket size finder</h2><p class="bs-p">Off-the-rack jackets are sized by chest and length. Enter two measurements to get a starting size, then let a tailor do the rest.</p></div>
<div class="bs-sz-g"><div class="bs-card"><label class="bs-lb" for="sz-c">Chest, around the fullest part: <b id="sz-cv">40 in</b></label><input type="range" id="sz-c" min="34" max="52" step="1" value="40" class="bs-rng">
<label class="bs-lb" for="sz-h">Height: <b id="sz-hv">5 ft 10 in</b></label><input type="range" id="sz-h" min="62" max="78" step="1" value="70" class="bs-rng">
<label class="bs-lb" for="sz-w">Waist: <b id="sz-wv">34 in</b></label><input type="range" id="sz-w" min="28" max="46" step="1" value="34" class="bs-rng"></div>
<div class="bs-ticket" aria-live="polite"><p class="bs-tk-k">Your starting size</p><p class="bs-tk-s" id="sz-s">40R</p><dl><div><dt>Length</dt><dd id="sz-l">Regular</dd></div><div><dt>Drop</dt><dd id="sz-d">6 in</dd></div><div><dt>Trouser waist</dt><dd id="sz-t">34</dd></div></dl><p class="bs-tk-n" id="sz-n"></p></div></div></div></section>

<section class="bs-s bs-cl" id="cloth"><div class="bs-w bs-cl-g"><div><p class="bs-ey">Tool two</p><h2 class="rv">Cloth picker</h2><p class="bs-p">Cloth weight and weave matter as much as cut. Choose the season and the occasion to see a sensible starting cloth.</p>
<p class="bs-lb">Season</p><div class="bs-seg" id="cl-a" role="group"><button type="button" data-v="0">Spring</button><button type="button" data-v="1">Summer</button><button type="button" data-v="2" class="on">Autumn</button><button type="button" data-v="3">Winter</button></div><p class="bs-lb">Occasion</p><div class="bs-seg" id="cl-b" role="group"><button type="button" data-v="0" class="on">Office</button><button type="button" data-v="1">Wedding</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Weekend</button><button type="button" data-v="3">Evening</button></div><div class="bs-cl-r" aria-live="polite"><h3 id="cl-t"></h3><p id="cl-d"></p><dl><div><dt>Weight</dt><dd id="cl-w"></dd></div><div><dt>Weave</dt><dd id="cl-v"></dd></div><div><dt>Colour</dt><dd id="cl-c"></dd></div></dl></div></div>
<div class="bs-bolt"><div class="bs-bolt-s" id="cl-s" role="img" aria-label="Cloth swatch preview"></div><div class="bs-bolt-tag"><span>Swatch</span><b id="cl-n">Worsted wool</b></div><figure class="bs-bolt-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1634225025766-45925be6c96d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="blue and white tweed cloth in close up" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="bs-s bs-pr"><div class="bs-w"><div class="bs-sh bs-sh-c"><p class="bs-ey">Six to ten weeks</p><h2 class="rv">From paper to person</h2></div><ol class="bs-steps stg"><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1771587756631-6cffb69fc434?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a person drawing on a paper clothing pattern" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><span>01</span><h3>The paper pattern</h3><p>Thirty or more measurements become a pattern drafted for one body only.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1537057039314-1105d990934c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a tailor sitting between two sewing machines" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><span>02</span><h3>The basted fitting</h3><p>A loosely tacked shell is tried on, marked with chalk and taken apart.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1753164597544-a2736833357e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a fashion design studio with sewing materials" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><span>03</span><h3>The finished fitting</h3><p>Final tweaks to sleeve pitch, length and balance before the last stitches.</p></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="bs-dt"><div class="bs-w bs-dt-g"><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1724745523440-e9a3982d8994?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=420&q=75" alt="an assortment of coloured buttons on a table" width="420" height="420" loading="lazy"></figure><div class="bs-dt-t rv"><p class="bs-sig">small things</p><h2>Horn buttons, silk thread, hand-felled seams</h2><p>Look closely at a bespoke garment and you will find details nobody else sees: a hand-sewn buttonhole, a lining felled with tiny stitches, a collar shaped with a hot iron.</p></div><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1767039362599-1b51a9c7abe8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=420&q=75" alt="spools of thread on a wooden rack" width="420" height="420" loading="lazy"></figure></div></section>

